class Solution {

    public void deleteNode(ListNode node) {

        node.val = node.next.val;      // Copy the next node's value into the current node

        node.next = node.next.next;    // Skip the next node, effectively deleting it

    }
}

How to remember:

Suppose the list is:

1 → 2 → 3 → 4
        ↑
      node

After line 1:

node.val = node.next.val;
1 → 2 → 4 → 4
        ↑
      node

After line 2:

node.next = node.next.next;
1 → 2 → 4
        ↑
      node
Interview trick
node.val = node.next.val;      // Don't delete this node; make it look like the next node

node.next = node.next.next;    // Remove the actual next node

This is the easiest way to remember the logic:

1st line: Copy the next node's data.
2nd line: Delete the next node by skipping it.
